{"title":"2023 USAJMO Problems/Problem 2","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_4_(Less_technical_bary)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4 (Less technical bary)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Solution_5_(Less_bashy_bary)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5 (Less bashy bary)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Solution_6_(complex)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 6 (complex)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>(Holden Mui) In an acute triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" />, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> be the midpoint of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/3/e33fe7d65facd8868f58b6e94ddc7f153a5a3f9f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{BC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"18\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be the foot of the perpendicular from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/3/e73bc78b745edf7fe1e55dbfc3d914190faf5015.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AM$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"35\" height=\"14\" />. Suppose that the circumcircle of triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/b/a7b510ddc7cf8a87b5cc0dd15adf8480cd2e6945.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABP$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> intersects line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> at two distinct points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/6/9866e3a998d628ba0941eb4fea0666ac391d149a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"18\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> be the midpoint of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/0/0400d2a78f3adac267e7621c65d063b35fe53ab1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AQ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"28\" height=\"19\" />. Prove that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/0/bd096f6d987ad71625f4170c44fd9d738b79e322.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$NB=NC$\" width=\"86\" height=\"12\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=f-d4mi-AyxQ\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=f-d4mi-AyxQ</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> be the foot of the altitude from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> onto <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />. We want to show that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/6/d066d7dbafb50ff40194cdb3db7fa51d8dce89f1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DM=MQ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"95\" height=\"18\" /> for obvious reasons. \n</p><p>Notice that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/f/c9f8d590d11df9d9402950c405ad0087d010d929.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ADPC$\" width=\"57\" height=\"13\" /> is cyclic and that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> lies on the radical axis of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/2/e32d658aa51e2d4c830f4d956ce8f76a2e0bc246.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(ABPQ)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"69\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/6/066c11891ed23332c5f3285df6b1641e203f64cf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(ADPC)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"74\" height=\"20\" />. By Power of a Point, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/6/0362b8e4641d3497f9e6993269fb7fb67249f7b3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(CM)(DM)=(BM)(MQ)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"220\" height=\"20\" />. As <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57e0eb8d7b4f725df74fabcdee6dcd761509a946.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BM=CM$\" width=\"92\" height=\"12\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/6/d066d7dbafb50ff40194cdb3db7fa51d8dce89f1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DM=MQ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"95\" height=\"18\" />, as desired. \n</p><p>- Leo.Euler\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Proceed by Barycentrics. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/2/642669c4f7c994be090dcf1e890170378bfb6289.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A=(1, 0, 0), B=(0, 1, 0), C=(0, 0, 1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"306\" height=\"20\" />. Let D be the foot of the altitude from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/b/c0ba7262d8023ce7ef14e564704d78c6b2c9e813.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D=(0:S_C:S_B)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"140\" height=\"20\" />. Then, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/3/273cb1cb1b3bf75359c0baf11effc7f34ee2839b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P= (t, 1, 1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"95\" height=\"20\" />. The equation of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/4/5b43d3bbf4c7063edb2c5bf0890ad7103d1f42a6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(ACP)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"58\" height=\"20\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/e/31e2c6d1ebef3edabe5ab33db48e817fd530f95f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[-a^2yz-b^2xz-c^2xy+(vy)(x+y+z)=0\\]\" width=\"339\" height=\"20\" />\nwhere <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/5/c055a7567a88e95d1cf8e61e1d4e463a2f6afff6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(t+2)v = t(b^2+c^2)+a^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"200\" height=\"21\" />. Then, the equation of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/0/38054f87ce27ca0068b0ed685d6809b70f85c17a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(ABP)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"55\" height=\"18\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/c/5fc30ecd38a894c86aa574e3b10c57a8d1006af6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[-a^2yz-b^2xz-c^2xy+(wz)(x+y+z)=0\\]\" width=\"343\" height=\"20\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/9/9195fcf938a907da6e099cfbeb17a48c74b750de.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(t+2)w = t(b^2+c^2)+a^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"204\" height=\"21\" />. Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/3/6835ed09358d04156b0f4924e23072bff2d7ef92.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$v=w$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"49\" height=\"10\" />. But D is also on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/4/5b43d3bbf4c7063edb2c5bf0890ad7103d1f42a6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(ACP)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"58\" height=\"20\" />, so we find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/9/8a98c9749642365fe48857127c12da9636b74dc5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$w=v=S_B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"96\" height=\"17\" />. Then, if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/a/68ac6bb3ef0e6eb7a98661933a54599207f57091.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q = (0:y_1: z_1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"126\" height=\"20\" />, we find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/2/5e2543c422063668b3584f72c862cb1a9b6e0e70.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y_1 = \\frac{w}{a^2} = \\frac{S_B}{a^2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"114\" height=\"39\" />. Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/9/239c00d568f1c88deb14060d31b0a5013e9b62b2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q=(0:S_B:a^2-S_B)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"178\" height=\"21\" />. Note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/d/ddd8948195fbfe77b4d8364191f23442db6634e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D+Q=(0:a^2:a^2)=M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"210\" height=\"21\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> is the midpoint of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/3/583c1f8bb951773b126ac286a7932d30ec1b46ba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DQ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"29\" height=\"16\" />. Thus, a homothety at Q of factor 2 maps <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/d/8dd718c98ea4f54b52dc87c5d208ff3411f21aca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M \\mapsto D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"65\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/8/268fe1457573de7e432015903d2e26ea4142531f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N\\mapsto A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/a/27a05033cfdb968b3348b9bfc8cd115fbb6dcc9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$MN \\perp BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"91\" height=\"14\" />, as needed. \n</p><p>Alternatively, one could continue with Barycentrics, finding <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/b/63b5a62ace9bd16faef218970864df309d9ecf39.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N=\\left(1:\\frac{S_B}{a^2}:1-\\frac{S_B}{a^2}\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"193\" height=\"45\" />. Then, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/c/62c858eb59c0c3bfe4af68361fd5051388156d26.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a^2(y-z)+x(b^2-c^2) = a^2(\\frac{2S_B}{a^2}-1)+(b^2-c^2)=2S_B-(a^2+c^2-b^2)=0\\]\" width=\"539\" height=\"37\" /> implying <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> is on the perpendicular bisector, as desired.\n</p><p>-sillybone\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The condition is solved only if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/d/87d67bf46f45c7330734f12c19fcba43404c234d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle{NBC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"64\" height=\"18\" /> is isosceles, which in turn only happens if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/f/31fc3d60a21c65a04974f46defd2d131f5c0111e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{MN}$\" width=\"36\" height=\"15\" /> is perpendicular to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/3/e33fe7d65facd8868f58b6e94ddc7f153a5a3f9f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{BC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"18\" />. \nNow, draw the altitude from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/3/e33fe7d65facd8868f58b6e94ddc7f153a5a3f9f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{BC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"18\" />, and call that point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />. Because of the Midline Theorem, the only way that this condition is met is if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/3/0a33969855e5d7551e0d6787777573226890146b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle{AXQ} \\sim \\triangle{NMQ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"153\" height=\"18\" />, or if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/0/7b07f14c61770fcf8a12f88efef076045f97c749.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{XM}=\\overline{MQ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"96\" height=\"21\" />.\n</p><p>By <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/b/b0b3dbb5e0c16cabfa02f10ace626714ac385dbd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AA$\" width=\"27\" height=\"13\" /> similarity, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/0/0c01d0b09ffbabb4399473fdb10ad100a96795d1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle{AXM} \\sim \\triangle{CPM}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"156\" height=\"18\" />. Using similarity ratios, we get that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/9/2591ce68ccaa29a14f2b2e8423191b43cff96a8f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\overline{AM}}{\\overline{XM}}=\\frac{\\overline{CM}}{\\overline{PM}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"104\" height=\"44\" />. Rearranging, we get that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/6/ad685ea4e1afc879672d9862b16995e2f574635c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AM} \\cdot \\overline{MP}=\\overline{XM} \\cdot \\overline{MC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"189\" height=\"18\" />. This implies that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/e/69e1fe7b717fcc82ea6f6387a10cd98aca60c7f4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AXPC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> is cyclic.\n</p><p>Now we start using Power of a Point. We get that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/8/738b191b5126c21355a53bec039968d8cdfc8ded.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{BX} \\cdot \\overline {XQ}= \\overline{AM} \\cdot \\overline{MP}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"181\" height=\"21\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/6/ad685ea4e1afc879672d9862b16995e2f574635c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AM} \\cdot \\overline{MP}=\\overline{XM} \\cdot \\overline{MC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"189\" height=\"18\" /> from before. This leads us to get that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/5/625f9ad15b0f56a7ff3800c88e208256ffabdffd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{BX} \\cdot \\overline {XQ}=\\overline{XM} \\cdot \\overline{MC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"184\" height=\"21\" />. \n</p><p>Now we assign variables to the values of the segments. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/4/924c1ac6c1a273082e0b2d31cba5579a2ccde29a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{BX}=a, \\overline{XM}=b, \\overline{MQ}=c,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"222\" height=\"21\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/4/a54aecdace997cacdfa8f3380947327da2a25a20.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{QC}=d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"64\" height=\"21\" />. The equation from above gets us that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/4/d045ba39a0618033560a142df75931bd5deea95f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a+b)c=b(c+d)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"149\" height=\"20\" />. As <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/4/1/141742d9ebf66b82ec079813e9f26862516ec432.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b=c+d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"103\" height=\"14\" /> from the problem statements, this gets us that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/d/ebda5306c70a24c574ef0107ed5b5152b5f594cf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b=c$\" width=\"40\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/5/045f52cb282e7f037f76676f4a22a19ae61a5f8b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{XC}=\\overline{CQ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"86\" height=\"21\" />, and we are done.\n</p><p>-dragoon and rhydon516 (:\n</p><p>note: i think a lot of places you used the wrong point names ~Aarush12\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_4_.28Less_technical_bary.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4_(Less_technical_bary)\">Solution 4 (Less technical bary)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4 (Less technical bary)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We are going to use barycentric coordinates on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/1/5c12b28a637be3bb4c707e2a5e4bce47aabeed31.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A=(1,0,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"94\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/1/c015abd5846b8538042d38f167ec4d3abb8b4bb2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B=(0,1,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"95\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/0/0601dfe585e5f1db64ff77ab451365145c24c9b2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C=(0,0,1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"94\" height=\"18\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/5/20520aed0f4d38d4ba63fdbf54491f0e4555b3c5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"65\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/0/4d0945ed672d46e0b3ce68eab77d3c8c97785ca4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b=CA$\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/4/114ba3529432afc9366c7bf2c908575b7f8ed901.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c=AB$\" width=\"59\" height=\"13\" />. We have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/b/1fb5112505bce7988d9cc8b91da48b484ab06729.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M=\\left(0,\\frac{1}{2},\\frac{1}{2}\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"123\" height=\"45\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/a/d6a80903db44d5eb62bb383a6511a5833a3526d8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P=(x:1:1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"113\" height=\"20\" /> so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/5/265432797fab2788235bc02940d95ca9d9b57d82.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overrightarrow{CP}=\\left(\\frac{x}{x+2},\\frac{1}{x+2},\\frac{1}{x+2}-1\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"265\" height=\"45\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/0/e506695b7c7d73acd8a66004cee5cb4ba53e34a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overrightarrow{AM}=\\left(-1,\\frac{1}{2},\\frac{1}{2}\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"151\" height=\"45\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/5/3b5bc4e868718f71c6bab0f1489cea52ccb6aa0b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overleftrightarrow{CP}\\perp\\overleftrightarrow{AM}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"88\" height=\"21\" />, it follows that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/7/8774a16099bf43614563e9f59b300ea161eb65e3.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} a^2\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot\\frac{1}{x+2}+\\frac{1}{2}\\left(\\frac{1}{x+2}-1\\right)\\right)+b^2\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot\\frac{x}{x+2}-\\left(\\frac{1}{x+2}-1\\right)\\right)\\\\ +c^2\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot\\frac{x}{x+2}-\\frac{1}{x+2}\\right)=0. \\end{align*}\" width=\"521\" height=\"92\" />\nSolving this gives\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/6/f46af55f622c06ea0c8f0b11db8e8844679eb110.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[ x=\\frac{2b^2-2c^2}{a^2-3b^2-c^2} \\]\" width=\"137\" height=\"39\" />\nso\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/3/b134fccca3069ac67bf46ab3c50eb22e82974883.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[ P=\\left(\\frac{b^2-c^2}{a^2-2b^2-2c^2},\\frac{a^2-3b^2-c^2}{2a^2-4b^2-4c^2},\\frac{a^2-3b^2-c^2}{2a^2-4b^2-4c^2}\\right). \\]\" width=\"448\" height=\"43\" />\nThe equation for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/0/38054f87ce27ca0068b0ed685d6809b70f85c17a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(ABP)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"55\" height=\"18\" /> is\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/4/0a431e6df8acb6e9f7331534548de50f87789bf9.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[ -a^2yz-b^2zx-c^2xy+ux+vy+wz=0. \\]\" width=\"329\" height=\"19\" />\nPlugging in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/0/980113411db28cef19af839a617cbfbc250a74dd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$u=v=0$\" width=\"77\" height=\"12\" />. Plugging in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> gives\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/5/5c51b92055f6630b6adee4b39574bdab97b62280.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} -a^2\\left(\\frac{a^2-3b^2-c^2}{2a^2-4b^2-4c^2}\\right)^2-b^2\\cdot\\frac{a^2-3b^2-c^2}{2a^2-4b^2-4c^2}\\cdot\\frac{b^2-c^2}{a^2-2b^2-2c^2}\\\\ -c^2\\cdot\\frac{b^2-c^2}{a^2-2b^2-2c^2}\\cdot\\frac{a^2-3b^2-c^2}{2a^2-4b^2-4c^2}+w\\cdot\\frac{a^2-3b^2-c^2}{2a^2-4b^2-4c^2}=0 \\end{align*}\" width=\"496\" height=\"92\" />\nso\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/c/cacc5ed4245e3142586554d67b96c9894eb26a51.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[ w=\\frac{2b^4-2c^4+a^4-3a^2b^2-a^2c^2}{2a^2-4b^2-4c^2}=\\frac{a^2}{2}-\\frac{b^2}{2}+\\frac{c^2}{2}. \\]\" width=\"401\" height=\"39\" />\nNow let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/d/9bd9f2dc5e7ef092528294ffa1db4f4cdc823892.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q=(0,t,1-t)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"124\" height=\"20\" /> where\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/5/40569ae868c107d288ca900bf4308a5ec3d06c4a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} -a^2t(1-t)+w(1-t)&amp;=0\\\\ \\implies t&amp;=\\frac{w}{a^2} \\end{align*}\" width=\"220\" height=\"61\" />\nso <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/a/4ea5d87a2a8f672ac53be2e61345323fd917bd3b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q=\\left(0,\\frac{w}{a^2},1-\\frac{w}{a^2}\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"160\" height=\"35\" />. It follows that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/2/9226706e7929581ce4f48af5e57b0d3de406b164.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N=\\left(\\frac{1}{2},\\frac{w}{2a^2},1-\\frac{w}{2a^2}\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"190\" height=\"45\" />. It suffices to prove that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/6/b5640aeb11cfa95574e7b2b1396db5e505663109.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overleftrightarrow{ON}\\perp\\overleftrightarrow{BC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"86\" height=\"21\" />. Setting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/e/6ee4e42bc5e7374f0b2b36b46cc2b7476dc93848.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overrightarrow{O}=0$\" width=\"51\" height=\"22\" />, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/8/5f875f10b1d091790d4916fef1fd7117a1de2d53.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overrightarrow{N}=\\left(\\frac{1}{2},\\frac{w}{2a^2},1-\\frac{w}{2a^2}\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"191\" height=\"45\" />. Furthermore we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/0/6c08f67143f71779e30f39ef699ba4d2e5139a7c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overrightarrow{CB}=(0,1,-1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"127\" height=\"25\" /> so it suffices to prove that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/f/bcf00717d151a33ae8a9e8342be0b6e3830aa19e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} a^2\\left(-\\frac{w}{2a^2}+\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{u}{2a^2}\\right)+b^2\\left(-\\frac{1}{2}\\right)+c^2\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)=0\\\\ \\implies w=\\frac{a^2}{2}-\\frac{b^2}{2}+\\frac{c^2}{2} \\end{align*}\" width=\"384\" height=\"88\" />\nwhich is valid. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/c/b6cf65b1f2fbdf388e3daeff9b96b34d3399d777.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\square$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>~KevinYang2.71\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_5_.28Less_bashy_bary.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5_(Less_bashy_bary)\">Solution 5 (Less bashy bary)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5 (Less bashy bary)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We employ barycentric coordinates. Set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/01927bf7bbcf5688067a91087d440c77879049b6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AMC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"49\" height=\"14\" /> as the reference triangle with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/9/5594734f575ba9bb2b41af9aebde75dcddb18834.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A = (1, 0, 0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"94\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/c/f5ce8d4cea17289b11560c07bef64662add5c36d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M = (0, 1, 0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"103\" height=\"20\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/f/c2fd56e5e6cc30249cdd51c3121d4622fdbc53a2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C = (0, 0, 1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"94\" height=\"18\" />. We immediately have,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/2/45202cdcf43c309fca11a82495e26ff159fdf443.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[P = (S_B : S_A : 0); B = (0, 2, -1)\\]\" width=\"253\" height=\"18\" />\nSince it passes through <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />, for some <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/3/1e32d8fab3a6be819121744a83223454c8626c15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$v, w$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"33\" height=\"13\" />, the equation of circle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/0/38054f87ce27ca0068b0ed685d6809b70f85c17a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(ABP)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"55\" height=\"18\" /> is,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/e/f2ef8946d24d1a87633a4d382aa87d20d4cda035.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(ABP): -a^2 yz - b^2 zx - c^2 xy + (vy + wz)(x + y + z) = 0\\]\" width=\"456\" height=\"20\" />\nPlugging in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/7/f074438404ac03d2f941bd628a83c8b6f41985b9.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[- c^2 S_{AB} + (v S_A)(c^2) = 0\\]\" width=\"190\" height=\"20\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/1/4d182d7a523813a4cd2cdee3e04b9515ba891a89.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\iff v = S_B\\]\" width=\"97\" height=\"15\" />\nPlugging in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/0/f708aff323dd08b3db9a250242b7eec560ca236e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2a^2 + (2v - w) = 0\\]\" width=\"149\" height=\"20\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55da59e5e00d72170b5b59f2df5be192175f4e1.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\iff 2a^2 + 2 S_B = 3 a^2 - b^2 + c^2 = w\\]\" width=\"285\" height=\"18\" />\nIn conclusion the circle has formula,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/f/91fd78b723ece5460835f195e46bd9e33b9ac125.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(ABP): -a^2 yz - b^2 zx - c^2 xy + ((S_B)y + (3 a^2 - b^2 + c^2) z)(x + y + z) = 0\\]\" width=\"538\" height=\"20\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/6/9866e3a998d628ba0941eb4fea0666ac391d149a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"18\" /> is the second intersection of circle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/0/38054f87ce27ca0068b0ed685d6809b70f85c17a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(ABP)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"55\" height=\"18\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/e/cbeda7159b33badd3617a005290a98fb0be341cb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{CM}$\" width=\"34\" height=\"15\" />. We let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/6/966f64e76775b3e71f90898a4472f4547173aefa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q = (0, 1 - t, t)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"124\" height=\"20\" /> for some <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/0/80008cbc162ed3b9cbfc7b14b760aa92cf163c88.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t \\neq -1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"56\" height=\"18\" />. Plugging this in,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/7/e57e1ecd99b6e5d80eca1444e73abf724258da23.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[-a^2 (1-t)t + ((S_B)(1-t) + (3 a^2 - b^2 + c^2) t) = 0\\]\" width=\"390\" height=\"20\" />\nWe claim that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/3/1638a55c5bc28591fc6b281f87c3d35fc070ebb5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t = -\\frac{S_B}{a^2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"73\" height=\"39\" /> is the other solution. \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/e/89e568df6522796ffc0a075fbd65b1cb1b5fc809.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\left(1+ \\frac{S_B}{a^2} \\right) S_B + \\left((S_B)\\left(1+ \\frac{S_B}{a^2}\\right) - (3 a^2 - b^2 + c^2) \\frac{S_B}{a^2}\\right) = 0\\]\" width=\"475\" height=\"43\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/c/54c6200b34a79dec091ffb91c70960bd8f068415.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\iff \\left(\\frac{3a^2 - b^2 + c^2}{2a^2} \\right) + \\left(\\left(\\frac{3a^2 - b^2 + c^2}{2a^2}\\right) - (3 a^2 - b^2 + c^2) \\frac{1}{a^2}\\right) = 0\\]\" width=\"536\" height=\"43\" />\nFactoring out the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/e/05e4947376055419bf672f5956c4ea5337cd2015.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{3a^2 - b^2 + c^2}{2a^2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"107\" height=\"41\" />, this is clearly true.\n</p><p>We also check that, these are not the same value.\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/0/080ebd41f5e536581a61fdb698dc397a690bb386.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[-\\frac{S_B}{a^2} = -1\\]\" width=\"85\" height=\"37\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/6/066c101dcd95e176ce93d33a36a5363774c49061.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\iff a^2 - b^2 + c^2 = 2a^2\\]\" width=\"183\" height=\"17\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/5/a653776eaf3942135e836bacbd1e84a4661a44b3.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\iff c^2 = a^2 + b^2\\]\" width=\"135\" height=\"17\" />\nThe triangle is acute, so this is impossible.\n</p><p>Since we had a quadratic in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/d/e0d2bf360290fd61d1c1557e763f2622363b3d35.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"13\" /> with at most two solutions, the second intersection <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/6/9866e3a998d628ba0941eb4fea0666ac391d149a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"18\" /> is indeed,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/2/c02425ab755c655c060d32d7e02e9b8b3fad414f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[Q = \\left( 0, 1 + \\frac{S_B}{a^2}, -\\frac{S_B}{a^2} \\right)\\]\" width=\"184\" height=\"43\" />\nTherefore,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/2/d42832af41854e6184ca734e6789b9f154227205.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[N = \\frac{A + Q}{2} = \\left( \\frac{1}{2}, \\frac{1}{2} - \\frac{S_B}{2a^2}, \\frac{S_B}{2a^2} \\right)\\]\" width=\"266\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p>~ Daniel Ge\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_6_.28complex.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_6_(complex)\">Solution 6 (complex)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 6 (complex)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/3/3431b35dcd263cac56e5c8a8aed399ba0ce6fce2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle AMC$\" width=\"63\" height=\"13\" /> to be unit circle, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/e/cbeda7159b33badd3617a005290a98fb0be341cb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{CM}$\" width=\"34\" height=\"15\" /> is horizontal.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/5/575d7ffc7c44d0647bc866ac2dee34fcc14108ab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A=a, C=c, M=-\\frac{1}{c}, P = \\frac{1}{2}(a+c+\\frac{a}{c^2}-\\frac{1}{c}), B = \\frac{-2}{c}-c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"478\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>Now we want to prove that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/0/480a7d3e1aaddbb7e44fd9bfbebdb2d96b083b04.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{NB}=\\overline{NC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"88\" height=\"18\" />, which really means that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> lies on the perpendicular bisector of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/3/e33fe7d65facd8868f58b6e94ddc7f153a5a3f9f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{BC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"18\" />. Now, shift the coordinate system by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/2/572eb883fe723c188762769b3bec495f055957ce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$+\\frac{1}{c}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"29\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/9/7e95b6b6889ef5c8135dfb9ad084ce7834bc73f0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A = a+\\frac{1}{c}, C = c+\\frac{1}{c}, M=0, P = \\frac{1}{2}(a+c+\\frac{a}{c^2}+\\frac{1}{c}), B = \\frac{-1}{c}-c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"530\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/8/b28877d5d3d2eac6a33bfe5dd75eb8dde09b34f3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N=ki$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"59\" height=\"14\" /> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/3/3d3e4f0b4707b434ca7642e7bd75f7bde46446b3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k\\in R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"48\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/f/f9fef1904c094e77f60f0d61654bc5332ea6985a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q=2ki-a-\\frac{1}{c}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"133\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>The imaginary part of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/4/93499acb9fa26a093e866ee073977ada1554777b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"47\" height=\"16\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/f/73f076c0f609930751d893de44b60b707e3bb4f3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2ki=\\frac{(a-\\frac{1}{a}+-c+\\frac{1}{c})}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"190\" height=\"42\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/7/1c78032cf043bc86d4c84318c18dae18bc6f2d70.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q = \\frac{-a-\\frac{1}{a}-c-\\frac{1}{c}}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"165\" height=\"42\" />\n</p><p><br />\n</p><p><br />\nNow all we need to do is to check that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/0/0b09aa4ade6fe6f89a53155dc605c43ff15244e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A,B,P,Q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"81\" height=\"18\" /> are conc-cyclic.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/3/fb38ffef5ae07e41eedaaa5dc137f0b444199ff4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{(A-P)(B-Q)}{(A-Q)(B-P)} \\in R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"172\" height=\"45\" />\n</p><p>Throwing out the half and some negative terms for simplicity.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/b/b1b94d695703edce5621f05fb07713037f731e5c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{(a+\\frac{1}{c}-c-\\frac{a}{c^2})({a+\\frac{1}{a}-c-\\frac{1}{c}})}{(3a+\\frac{3}{c}+\\frac{1}{a} + c)(\\frac{3}{c}+3c+a+\\frac{a}{c^2})} \\in R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"306\" height=\"49\" />\n</p><p><br />\nSo we need to prove that:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/9/d09a63e60ceff9d0702275469194b2303c10d4f8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{(a+\\frac{1}{c}-c-\\frac{a}{c^2})({a+\\frac{1}{a}-c-\\frac{1}{c}})}{(3a+\\frac{3}{c}+\\frac{1}{a} + c)(\\frac{3}{c}+3c+a+\\frac{a}{c^2})} =\\frac{(\\frac{1}{a}+c-\\frac{1}{c}-\\frac{c^2}{a})({a+\\frac{1}{a}-c-\\frac{1}{c}})}{(\\frac{3}{a}+3c+a + \\frac{1}{c})(3c+\\frac{3}{c}+\\frac{1}{a}+\\frac{c^2}{a})}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -21px\" width=\"563\" height=\"53\" />\n</p><p><br />\nOn the RHS, we can multiply the numerator and denominator by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/6/8362dd17da7c07cedd4018d589a0b21e9575e287.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{a}{c}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"12\" height=\"33\" /> to get:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/3/82390963c07640d84833bd601f090ab7f526324c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(3a+\\frac{3}{c}+\\frac{1}{a} + c)(\\frac{3}{c}+3c+a+\\frac{a}{c^2})=(\\frac{3}{a}+3c+a + \\frac{1}{c})(3a+\\frac{3a}{c^2}+\\frac{1}{c}+c)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"577\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/5/db58757966924b5015ffd70aa77ab2535d736752.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(3+\\frac{c}{a})(a+\\frac{1}{c})(3+\\frac{a}{c})(c+\\frac{1}{c})=(a+\\frac{1}{c})(1+\\frac{3c}{a})(c+\\frac{1}{c})(\\frac{3a}{c}+1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"511\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/0/d503b8ba7cc34581abb5e9d53b5bbe4b19f2b2d6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(3+\\frac{c}{a})(3+\\frac{a}{c})=(1+\\frac{3c}{a})(\\frac{3a}{c}+1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"279\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>Which is true if you multiply <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/f/90fe8263dd262c6d4d42e5e955afefd6adc0917c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ac$\" width=\"17\" height=\"8\" /> on both sides. Thus, we are done (note we could have factored earlier which would have saved tremendous time).\n</p><p>~MATHLOVERSSD\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:40%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_USAJMO\" title=\"2023 USAJMO\">2023 USAJMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_USAJMO_Problems\" title=\"2023 USAJMO Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=176&amp;year=2023\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2023 USAJMO Problems/Problem 1\">Problem 1</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2023 USAJMO Problems/Problem 3\">Problem 3</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2023 USAJMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2023 USAJMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2023 USAJMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2023 USAJMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2023 USAJMO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=USAJMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"USAJMO Problems and Solutions\"> All USAJMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018024143\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.070 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.097 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 866/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1326/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 48/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 31581/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   20.120      1 -total\n 71.16%   14.317      1 Template:USAJMO_newbox\n 27.35%    5.503      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:24152:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018024143 and revision id 286449. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}